/-
# N280 — THE TWO-HANDED so(4) = su(2)_L ⊕ su(2)_R OF THE MATTER SPINOR,
#         CONFINED TO THE LAST ASSOCIATIVE RUNG H, BROKEN ON O BY THE CASCADE-STOPPING ASSOCIATOR

Over the DERIVED octonion rung `O ℚ = CD (H ℚ)` (the terminal cascade algebra, N2c) and its matter
SPINOR structure (`leftReg`/`rightReg`, N261/N264: `O ℚ` a Clifford module for the fold's Born form
`gForm` under BOTH multiplication faces). GATHER-native (the obstruction to closure/fusion IS the
gather gluing obstruction / associator, N219 / N262 `spinGen` / N264 `chir_mixed_apply`).

N279 put the weak-isospin FUNDAMENTAL doublet on the matter spinor as the LEFT-regular action
`leftReg a = (a·−)` of the last-doubled H-imaginary units — but built the LEFT face ONLY. N264 PROVED
the fold's worldMap is intrinsically TWO-HANDED (both `leftReg`/`rightReg` are Clifford modules,
non-fusable). THIS node completes the two-handed object: the RIGHT-regular action is EQUALLY a
fundamental su(2)_R doublet, and — on the last associative rung H — the two hands COMMUTE, assembling
the `so(4) = su(2)_L ⊕ su(2)_R` (the rotation algebra of the associative rung realized as
left/right multiplication). On the full non-associative `O ℚ`, NEITHER hand closes and the two do
NOT commute, all three failures equal to (−2•) the banked associator — so the entire two-handed
`so(4)` is CONFINED to H and BROKEN on O by the SAME non-associativity that stops the cascade.

## The objects (all derived, foundations-only)
  · `rregI`/`rregJ`/`rregK := rightReg u1M/e2I/e3I` — the RIGHT-regular operators of the H-units.
  · ★★★ `rightmul_comm_obstruction` — the RIGHT commutator obstruction `= -2•assoc`, coordinate-free
        from the banked `assoc_swap23` (the MIRROR of N279's `leftmul_comm_obstruction` from
        `assoc_swap12`). The failure of the right-regular commutator to be the right-regular of the
        algebra commutator IS twice the banked associator (the gather gluing obstruction N219 / N264).
  · ★★ `rightReg_closure_on_H_IJ` — su(2)_R CLOSES on H: `⁅R_hI,R_hJ⁆ = -2•R_hK` (OPPOSITE
        orientation to su(2)_L's `+2`, the L/R sign that distinguishes the two hands).
  · ★★★ `leftRight_commute_on_H` — the LEFT and RIGHT su(2)'s COMMUTE on the H-image
        (`⁅L_hI, R_hJ⁆ = 0`): the associator vanishing on H (`assoc_iotaO`) is exactly what lets the
        two hands assemble the `so(4) = su(2)_L ⊕ su(2)_R` there.
  · ★★ `rightReg_casimir_eq_neg_three` — the RIGHT doublet Casimir `-3•id` (spin-½, via `rightReg_sq`).
  · ★★★ `rightReg_defect_eq_associator` + W8 `rightReg_comm_obstructed` — su(2)_R FAILS to close on
        `O` by exactly `-2•assoc` — BOTH hands confined to H by the SAME associator.
  · ★★★ `so4_breaks_on_O` — the two hands do NOT commute on the non-associative `O ℚ` (banked N264
        `chir_spinor_block`): the whole `so(4)` is torn apart off H.
  · `lregI_ne_rregI` — the two hands are genuinely DISTINCT operators (non-vacuity).
  · ★★★ CAPSTONE `two_handed_so4_structure`.

## THE DISSOLUTION / MOAT (load-bearing novelty — NOT the generic so(4))
The generic `so(4) ≅ su(2) × su(2)` of quaternion left/right multiplication is a textbook fact about
associative `H`, and the ADJOINT/derivations realization inside `g₂ = Der(O ℚ)` is already banked
(N191, `DerivationSO4TwoSU2`, a NON-breaking Lie subalgebra). What is NEW and fold-SPECIFIC here is:
(i) the FUNDAMENTAL realization on the actual matter SPINOR `O ℚ` (as different from N191's adjoint
as N279's fundamental doublet is from N277's adjoint triplets); and (ii) the CONFINEMENT of the
two-handed `so(4)` to the last associative rung H and its BREAKING on the terminal algebra O by the
SAME non-associativity that stops the cascade (N2c), caps generations (N5), and blocks the chirality
fusion (N264). The field POSITS two chiralities as separate Weyl irreps; the theory reads matter's
two-handedness off the ONE worldMap's two multiplication faces, forming `so(4)` on H, torn apart on
O by the cascade stop — one cause, the ★3↔cascade-stop↔★6 joint, on the actual matter spinor.

## SCOPE — HONESTY CLAUSE
Banks the two-handed `so(4)` FUNDAMENTAL realization on the spinor + su(2)_R closure/Casimir/opposite-
orientation + the commuting-on-H (`so(4)`) + BOTH defects = the associator + the confinement/breaking
+ the one-cause tie ONLY. Does NOT derive PARITY VIOLATION (a SYMMETRIC `so(4)` is parity-CONSERVING;
which hand the weak force couples to stays the OPEN ★6 asymmetry — NOT claimed, NOT dressed up), NOT
the ℤ₂ involution grading (`L_{u1}∘R_{u1}` — its eigenspaces are N266's colour-neutral core, NOT new),
NOT the hypercharge NORMALIZATION / weak mixing angle (★2, ceiling STANDS — `Q ∉ span{T3,Y}`,
`[Q,Y] ≠ 0`; nothing childed toward it), NOT the ★5 texture (un-forceable, N275/N276), NOT
masses/mixings, NOT "= a specific SM chirality multiplet" (removable prose).

## Physics-words-removable (STANDARD §2)
Delete chirality/handed/left/right-handed/Weyl/parity/weak/isospin/matter/spinor/doublet: what remains
is a pure theorem — the left- and right-regular actions of the three imaginary units of the associative
subalgebra `H ⊂ O ℚ` give two 3-element families of endomorphisms of `O ℚ`; on the `H`-image each
family's commutators close into `su(2)` (structure constants `+2`/`-2`), each has square-sum `-3•id`,
and the two families mutually commute (`so(4)`); on the full `O ℚ` neither family closes and the two
do not commute, all three failures equal to `-2•` the banked associator. Octonion-SPECIFIC: the
closure/obstruction/commuting split IS the associative/non-associative boundary of the cascade. NOT
free-floating: every headline TYPE mentions the banked `leftReg`/`rightReg`/`O ℚ`/`assoc`/`u1`/`e2O`/
`e3O`/`iotaO`. Foundations-only: `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.
-/
import Phys.Algebra.TowerWorldMapWeakDoubletLeftRegular
import Phys.Algebra.TowerWorldMapChirality
import Mathlib.Tactic

